cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ck3bench in research, please cite it as below."
title: "ck3bench: Crusader Kings III as an environment for LLM agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stebbins
    given-names: Harrison
version: 2026.12.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3bench"
url: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3bench"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - game AI
  - Crusader Kings III
  - reinforcement learning
  - multi-agent environments
  - LLM agents
abstract: >-
  ck3bench is an environment for LLM agents over Crusader Kings III. Agents
  are seats (rulers in a running game) whose actions are typed tool calls on
  the ck3agent toolkit; one step is one decision cycle of game-days; rewards
  are read from game state. It offers a parallel multi-agent API with
  environment-owned messages and notepads and team rewards, a fake backend
  for tests, an HTTP server for policies in any language, a reference
  tool-calling agent, a mixed-policy runner, an MCP shim for a Claude Code
  seat, a JSONL trajectory format and an unsteered baseline.
